  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in the unjustified loss of existing office space as the applicant has failed to provide robust, site-specific marketing evidence to demonstrate that the premises are no longer viable or capable of continued office use. The limited information provided does not meet the requirement of policy 16 of the Sutton Local Plan (2018) and the proposal is therefore unacceptable, being contrary to policy 16.",
    "The proposed development would provide an unbalanced mix of dwellings sizes with only one of the four units being three bedroom (25% provision), falling short of the 50% three-bedroom provision required in accrodance with policy 9 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "Due to the size and design of the extensions, they appear excessive, disproportionate and as an overdevelopment of the site, and are generally incongruous within the setting to the detriment of the area. The proposed rear elevation would have a mix of stepped elevations, recesses, roof shapes, balconies and screening that would appear discordant and the proposed rear dormer would appear to fill the enitre roof slope, appearing top heavy, overly dominant and box-like. The proposed size, scale, bulk, mass and detailed design is therefore unacceptable as it would cause harm to the character of the streetscene and wider area, contrary to policy D3 of the London Plan 2018 and policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The proposed units misrepresent their true potential occupancy (showing double bedspaces as single bedspaces), and when assessed on the likely true occupancy the units would fail to meet the required space standards as set out at Table 3.1 of the London Plan. It is therefore considered that the proposal would provide a poor standard of accommodation for future occupants, contrary to policy D6 of the London Plan and policy 9 of the Sutton Local Plan."
  ],
